            "status": "partial",
            "error": null,
            "information": "**Answer (based on the evidence provided in the page text)**\n\nI wasn’t able to locate the award name that funded the 2019 paper about the radionuclide therapy in the page’s content. The page provides a link to the article on *Lutathera* (Lutetium‑177 DOTATATE), but it does not include the acknowledgments section or any mention of a specific funding award.\n\n**Why this conclusion?**\n\n| Evidence | Finding |\n|----------|---------|\n| The page contains a link titled \"`Lutathera (Lutetium Lu 177 Dotatate) First Radioactive Drug Approved for Gastroenteropancreatic Neuroendocrine Tumors`\" | Confirms the drug referenced is Lutathera (Lu‑177 DOTATATE). |\n| No text excerpt of the article or acknowledgments section was included in the page text | No location to read the award detail. |\n| The rest of the page lists many other drug‑approval articles, but none contain an award statement. | No award mention in this source. |\n\n**Clues for further searching**\n\n- The paper you’re looking for is likely titled or related to “Lutathera” or “Lutetium‑177 DOTATATE” and was published online in 2019 with four authors from three departments in a North American institution.  \n- The acknowledgments of that paper should include a funding award; common such awards for oncology research in the United States include the NIH R01, NCI Cancer Center Support Grant (CCSG), or the National Institutes of Health.  \n\nIf you can locate the PDF or the PubMed record of the paper, the acknowledgments section should list the specific award name (e.g., “National Cancer Institute grant P01‐CA209\\, etc.”).",
